factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The reel_script says the Vishnupathi punya kalam was observed on 'Tuesday' in the current year alongside the dates Feb 13, May 15, Aug 17 as if all were listed, but the article lists Feb 13, May 15, Aug 17 and 'Tuesday' only as observance days; the draft presents Tuesday as one of the observance dates in the same sentence, which is a mixing of facts but largely matches the article.
  The reel_script states the Tuesday temple visit was 'காலை' (morning) and that devotees gathered 'அதிகாலை முதலே' — consistent with the article, so no issue there.
  The reel_script omits the article's explanation that Krishna taught Arjuna about the significance of time in the Mahabharata war and that Vishnupathi punya kalam is linked to Surya's movement, and that dharma done in this time brings clarity and a prosperous life; this is an important element of the article's message that is missing.
  The reel_script says 'பக்தர்கள் கோயிலை' fine, but the phrase 'வண்ண மலர்களால் கோயில் அலங்காரம் செய்யப்பட்டு' changes the article: the article says the utsava deity and Thayar were decorated with colourful flowers, not the temple itself.
  The reel_script and caption say the Vishnupathi punya kalam 'வைகுண்டத்தின் கதவுகள் திறந்திருப்பதாக' — this matches the article, but the reel_script adds 'இந்த காலத்தில் வைக்கும் வேண்டுதல்கள் கட்டாயம் நிறைவேறும் என்பது பக்தர்களின் நம்பிக்கை' which is attributed to devotees while the article attributes it to belief generally; acceptable.
